with very, very common endings across different books.

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:59.080
He quoted the famous phrase lobsang gyel we ten pa (BLO BZANG RGYAL BA'I BSTAN PA) chik (CIG)

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:04.040
may the teachings of the victorious

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:07.000
Lobsang Drakpa Je Tsongkhapa be

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:09.480
spread throughout this world.

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:14.040
You think we should go online.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:17.400
We must translate this lamrim into many languages.

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:23.000
We must try to reach as many people as possible with the good word.

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:32.600
This is the end of the prayer and we must exit this lamrim video class

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:37.200
and we must start sharing the Dharma with other people.

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:39.720
We must spread Dharma in the world.

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:45.680
In this part of the lamrim, Pabongka Rinpoche said,

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:52.160
“The place where you should spread the Dharma is here, in your own heart.”

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:57.560
Don't think that spreading Dharma means trying to translate videos

00:11:57.560 --> 00:12:02.120
into other languages ​​or anything like that.  This is a very important dissemination of Dharma.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:06.680
But he says, "If you spread it in your own heart,

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:11.280
then of course it will spread beyond you, because peace comes from your heart,

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:13.000
from your heart chakra, actually.

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:18.200
Next picture #7

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:24.720
Try to remember what that picture was about. I'll give you a second.

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:33.000
This is my favorite theme;

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:43.400
to have a personal relationship with another person, like these two people have.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:49.200
In my opinion, and in Tantra, it is one of the happiest things that can happen to you.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:53.200
It is one of the greatest things that can happen to you.

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:59.000
Anyone can tell you the reason why the whole world is looking for a partner -

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:01.480
it makes people happy.

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:04.720
It is a great happiness when things go well.

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:09.000
It is one of the greatest happinesses you can have, but

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:14.120
you know and I know when things don't go well -

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:17.560
it is one of the greatest misfortunes in life.

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:21.200
Why is this relevant to this course in particular?

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:30.520
If your morals are good -

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:32.800
that is the happiest thing in your life.

00:13:33.400 --> 00:13:38.440
And if you violate your morals, that is the same thing that will  you unhappy.

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:41.760
It's like having a good woman or man who is your partner,

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:46.120
the same person who makes you completely happy

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:49.200
can also make you completely unhappy.

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:53.840
So in this case, the Vinaya, your personal practice of kindness,

00:13:54.320 --> 00:13:57.680
good behavior, is compared to a partner

00:13:57.680 --> 00:14:01.120
who can either make you the best in your life

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:04.760
or the worst in your life – one and the same person.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:11.520
Next Idima 8.

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:15.200
This one was difficult. See if you can remember?

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.000
I'll take a sip of my green drink.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:22.160
Thank you, Vimala.

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:35.040
This actually means breaking your commitments.

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:41.040
Pulling a weed means breaking your commitments.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:46.680
Why does destroying this plant violate your commitments?

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:53.040
If you are a gardener, you know that you must pull the weed

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:56.160
before the seeds ripen.

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:00.920
If you wait until the seeds ripen

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:03.280
and then pull the plant,

00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:06.040
you will scatter about a thousand seeds.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:12.680
Next month or next year, you will have thousands of weeds growing.

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.920
So you must attack these weeds in advance.

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:20.560
This refers to a very radical statement

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:22.800
that the Buddha made.  It is

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:29.240


00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:31.680
better to die

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:33.960
than to break your commitments. Why?

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:37.000
When you break your commitments,

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:40.360
you set in motion seeds

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:44.160
that will continue to be sown for many lifetimes.

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:51.080
If you die, you destroy one body-mind complex.

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:55.440
If you die, you destroy one very useful temple, the

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:58.800
physical temple and mind. You lose one.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:02.040
But if you break your commitments,

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:05.920
you lose many body-mind complexes.

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:08.920
You destroy your body and mind over many lifetimes.

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:12.920
And you are, as it were, setting in motion seeds

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:15.720
that will destroy many lifetimes.

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:21.880
The Buddha said, "It is better to die than to break your vows."

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:28.920
And he was not being metaphorical at all. He was speaking very literally

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:32.720
when he said that. It is better to die than to break your commitments.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:36.800
There is a joke in lam-rim.

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:45.760
We take a vow never to give up  bodhicitta, even at the cost of our own lives.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:53.960
There's a famous saying that we wait our whole lives for some evil people to

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:56.040
put us in jail

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:58.240
.

00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:03.960
They come with a knife and say, "Give up your bodhisattva vows or die today."

00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:06.120
Then we say,

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:07.960
"I choose death."

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:10.600
And they kill us.

00:17:11.080 --> 00:17:14.720
I think we've all been waiting for this since we took our vows.

00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:19.720
We're all waiting for these guys to show up with knives and threaten us.

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:24.320
But in reality, we are the guys with knives. We threaten our bodhisattva vows every day.

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:33.200
We have to make that decision every day when we decide whether or not to keep our vows carefully.

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:39.200
It's hard to find those guys who would put you in jail and say,

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:42.920
"I'll kill you if you don't give up your bodhisattva commitments."

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:48.040
Next picture.

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:56.040
See if you can remember. I'll give you a minute to try to remember.

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:07.200
That was a mention...

00:18:07.400 --> 00:18:10.440
We have a team of translators called Mixed Nuts,

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:14.040
and we were translating an old Vinaya text, the

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:17.920
vows of monks and nuns.

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:26.560
They were talking about vows, about a tradition that we shouldn't...

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:31.160
...when you become a monk or a nun, they give you your monastic robes,

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:33.200
they give you a small Buddhist statue,

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:36.320
and a strainer.

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:40.720
And in ancient India, it was believed that you should always carry this strainer with you.

00:18:41.480 --> 00:18:44.800
When you drink water from a stream,

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:50.920
you should first strain the water to make sure you don't kill any small insects.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:57.000
We mentioned a famous tradition in the Vinaya,

00:18:57.680 --> 00:19:00.680
if a couple of monks go down to the water,

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:03.840
down to the stream for water,

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:08.800
then they should choose the most responsible monk to test the water.

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:16.440
Don't choose the guy who doesn't care about bugs. Try to find a guy who likes bugs.

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:20.720
And let him test the water, because he'll be more careful.

00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:23.400
What's the point of that?

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:27.920
We were talking about peculiar ecological vows,

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:33.040
where monks and nuns  You shouldn't even pick the green leaves from the

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:39.040
plants because they are the homes of tiny creatures.

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:44.400
This means respecting even the smallest vows,

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:50.600
taking them very seriously because the results multiply exponentially. It

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:55.080
's also important to keep your morality on a very subtle level,

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:59.840
on a very subtle level, and not become meticulous.

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:04.040
If I were going to write bodhisattva commitments,

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:06.040
I would write an additional bodhisattva vow about

00:20:06.440 --> 00:20:08.600
not becoming meticulous about bodhisattva vows.

00:20:09.200 --> 00:20:11.200
There is nothing more annoying than

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:15.880
a person who tells you that he will keep his vows and

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:19.080
that's why they look like jerks today.

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:24.600
Keep your vows gently. Keep them joyfully. Don't overdo it.

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:31.080
Don't bother other people with your vows because vows shouldn't bother other people.

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:36.720
Keep small vows, keep them quietly. Keep them privately, don't advertise it.

00:20:37.760 --> 00:20:43.560
There is a saying in Islam, "The left hand should not speak to the right hand about  What she does."

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:48.120
What it means is, don't advertise your vows. Just keep them quietly.

00:20:48.920 --> 00:20:51.200
Keep them on a very subtle level.

00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:54.040
Next picture.

00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:06.120
This is the idea that being kind to other people

00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:10.240
is like planting a tree.

00:21:10.600 --> 00:21:13.400
Today I went to the Peach Tree Cafe

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:16.080
to check out something, and

00:21:17.400 --> 00:21:20.440
Stanley, Alison, and I planted a peach tree there

00:21:22.160 --> 00:21:25.080
when we first started the Peach Tree morning show.

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:29.760
And I want to tell you guys, three peaches have ripened this week, so

00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:32.800
we have peaches now. What

00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:40.160
it means is, take care of your core practice.

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:44.560
Take care of the root and plant good karma

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:47.920
by keeping your vows, by being kind to other people.

00:21:47.920 --> 00:21:49.960
Then it will grow into a tree.

00:21:50.440 --> 00:21:52.440
And this peach tree that we planted

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:55.080
five months ago or so is

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:58.040
already bearing a lot of fruit.

00:21:58.600 --> 00:22:05.040
If you hadn't taken care of it when it was tiny, you wouldn't have anything.

00:22:05.040 --> 00:22:08.200
If you take care of your core Buddhist practice,

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:10.800
which means being kind to others  people,

00:22:11.400 --> 00:22:14.120
then there will be thousands and thousands and thousands of fruits.

00:22:14.200 --> 00:22:16.160
They will appear, it will grow

00:22:16.160 --> 00:22:18.160
into a huge... it will grow into a tree

00:22:18.600 --> 00:22:23.480
and it will bear peaches every year, for many years you will have peaches.

00:22:24.160 --> 00:22:25.560
Take care.... protect....

00:22:25.760 --> 00:22:29.560
this child carefully protected the sprout.

00:22:29.960 --> 00:22:31.960
Protect your morality.

00:22:32.520 --> 00:22:34.520
Next picture.

00:22:36.240 --> 00:22:41.320
If I remember correctly, there were four conditions

00:22:42.240 --> 00:22:45.080
that could cause you to break your commitments.

00:22:45.080 --> 00:22:47.080
If you took the bodhisattva commitments

00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:50.440
or you took the Vinaya Pratimoksha commitments,

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:53.840
or even if you took the Diamond Way tantric commitments.

00:22:54.800 --> 00:23:00.200
I think there were four.. Pabongka Rinpoche went over... maybe even more....

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:02.920
anyway, there were certain conditions

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:05.080
that contributed to breaking your vows.

00:23:05.160 --> 00:23:09.240
If you want to break your vows, there are a few specific ways to do it.

00:23:09.240 --> 00:23:10.320
Here is the first one.

00:23:11.080 --> 00:23:16.440
If you don't know what your vows are,

00:23:17.120 --> 00:23:21.000
then this is a good way to break them. If you want to break them,

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:22.720
then don't study them and,

00:23:23.160 --> 00:23:27.080
one of them really irritates me,  I have a lot of Dharma irritants, and they are

00:23:28.160 --> 00:23:33.800
teachers who give initiations, initiations to the masses,

00:23:33.800 --> 00:23:38.600
and they don’t explain to the people taking the initiation

00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:41.520
that they have just taken vows.

00:23:41.560 --> 00:23:44.840
There are hundreds of vows that you took when you received initiation,

00:23:45.760 --> 00:23:48.320
and you will definitely break them if you don’t know them.

00:23:48.320 --> 00:23:51.120
It is the teacher’s responsibility

00:23:52.120 --> 00:23:55.400
to teach you your vows before you receive initiation.

00:23:56.320 --> 00:24:01.080
If they don’t offer to teach you, I would not take initiation from them.

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:07.080
The best way to break your vows, the first way, is not to know them.

00:24:07.560 --> 00:24:09.400
Read the recipe before you start cooking.

00:24:10.240 --> 00:24:12.720
That’s what Veronica tells me every time I cook.

00:24:14.160 --> 00:24:16.160
Next picture.

00:24:17.000 --> 00:24:23.360
This woman says, “Yeah, it’s not such a big deal.”

00:24:23.560 --> 00:24:33.600
It’s a vow not to cut green plants without prayer,

00:24:34.320 --> 00:24:40.400
okay, that’s an extreme. It’s a little excessive, it’s not that big of a deal.

00:24:40.400 --> 00:24:43.000
It’s just a couple of bugs

00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:47.560
that sometimes use this leaf as a roof.

00:24:47.560 --> 00:24:50.040
It’s not that big of a deal.

00:24:50.480 --> 00:24:53.800
The second great way to break your vows

00:24:54.040 --> 00:24:55.400
is to have this attitude:

00:24:55.400 --> 00:24:59.200
“Oh, this one doesn’t  so important, I keep big ones."

00:25:00.200 --> 00:25:02.120
Next.

00:25:06.240 --> 00:25:12.400
If we get a kleshe, that is, if we get some kind of negativity

00:25:12.800 --> 00:25:16.920
that swirls in our minds, that's a great way to break your vows.

00:25:17.080 --> 00:25:20.600
Being mad at someone else or

00:25:21.080 --> 00:25:26.280
being obsessed with something or money or

00:25:26.600 --> 00:25:29.480
being addicted to our Netflix at night.

00:25:30.040 --> 00:25:36.000
.... by the way, there's nothing wrong with watching Netflix, but I'm talking about

00:25:38.960 --> 00:25:43.200
not hurting someone else because you want to come home and watch your Netflix. That's the problem.

00:25:44.800 --> 00:25:46.920
It's called a gang fight.

00:25:46.920 --> 00:25:48.320
What's the story?

00:25:52.120 --> 00:25:56.040
Go to the biggest guy on the opposing side.

00:25:57.000 --> 00:25:59.000
Find out who the leader is on the other side

00:25:59.560 --> 00:26:04.080
and don't talk, don't negotiate, don't yell at each other,

00:26:04.080 --> 00:26:07.000
go up to him and hit him over the head.

00:26:07.480 --> 00:26:10.800
And then the whole other side will collapse.

00:26:11.080 --> 00:26:15.080
Identify your worst bad habit

00:26:15.080 --> 00:26:19.000
and deal with it first. That's the way to keep your vows.

00:26:19.760 --> 00:26:21.760
Next.

00:26:25.240 --> 00:26:30.640
By the way, at my age,

00:26:30.640 --> 00:26:33.760
I'll tell you how old I am,

00:26:33.760 --> 00:26:37.080
but all this young love stuff

00:26:37.080 --> 00:26:40.160
– they're so ridiculous from my age's perspective.

00:26:42.320 --> 00:26:44.800
I can say this from experience, because I've had it.

00:26:46.320 --> 00:26:48.240
But this thing about:

00:26:48.240 --> 00:26:50.800
"Oh, she's the most beautiful woman in the world.

00:26:51.400 --> 00:26:53.400
He's the most handsome guy in the world."

00:26:54.440 --> 00:26:59.560
First of all, my older brother,

00:26:59.560 --> 00:27:02.920
he said the funniest thing. "Do you like this girl?" he asked. "Yes," I said. "Do

00:27:03.480 --> 00:27:05.480
you want to spend your whole life with her?" "Yes," I said.

00:27:06.160 --> 00:27:08.160
He said, "Check her mother first.

00:27:09.000 --> 00:27:16.120
Look at what her mom looks like?" I said mom looks terrible. She's overweight, she looks tired, and she looks terrible.

00:27:16.920 --> 00:27:21.800
And he said, "Well, what do you think she looked like in the beginning?"

00:27:22.040 --> 00:27:24.240
So think about it?

00:27:25.480 --> 00:27:29.560
If you're attached to a person's appearance,

00:27:30.240 --> 00:27:35.280
or anything physical, or anything not very important about a person.

00:27:35.480 --> 00:27:41.120
That will change, and you'll see them get sick,

00:27:41.120 --> 00:27:44.000
you'll see them age. You'll see them have diarrhea and vomit.

00:27:44.240 --> 00:27:48.040
If you're unlucky, you'll see their insides someday during surgery.

00:27:49.080 --> 00:27:52.120
Don't kid yourself that it's

00:27:53.080 --> 00:27:55.080
worth hurting other people

00:27:55.760 --> 00:28:00.680
to get the most beautiful woman or man possible. It's not worth it.

00:28:01.960 --> 00:28:08.600
It won't last. It's great to be in a relationship, but have it with the right motivation.

00:28:09.200 --> 00:28:11.200
Next.

00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:15.080
If you have anger issues

00:28:16.160 --> 00:28:18.160
or you get upset quickly,

00:28:18.320 --> 00:28:21.080
then fantasize about giving that person

00:28:21.760 --> 00:28:25.480
something they would like to have. It's  called maitre

00:28:26.120 --> 00:28:27.480
jampa

00:28:27.480 --> 00:28:28.120
love.

00:28:28.120 --> 00:28:33.400
Fantasy, try to remember how nice it is to give someone

00:28:34.040 --> 00:28:36.160
something they love, something they want.

00:28:36.200 --> 00:28:38.240
Try to have that attitude.

00:28:38.720 --> 00:28:42.040
If you don't feel friendly towards the other person, then

00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:45.880
fantasize about doing a meditation

00:28:47.000 --> 00:28:50.440
on giving them something they really like.

00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:53.000
Next.

00:28:54.040 --> 00:29:00.040
I'll give you a minute on this. I'm sure you don't remember what that is?

00:29:01.480 --> 00:29:03.400
Tim cheats by looking ahead.

00:29:08.040 --> 00:29:10.040
What was that?

00:29:11.080 --> 00:29:13.960
It's about pride.

00:29:14.720 --> 00:29:17.840
Pride will also be an obstacle to fulfilling your vows.

00:29:18.720 --> 00:29:22.120
And... one of the most common types of pride

00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:28.040
in the monastic environment where this book was typically taught

00:29:30.320 --> 00:29:35.280
is how much you know about the scriptures, how many facts you've collected

00:29:36.040 --> 00:29:37.120
over your life. What

00:29:37.400 --> 00:29:41.280
I really like is the obscure facts of the Dharma

00:29:41.280 --> 00:29:43.080
and the more you collect,

00:29:43.480 --> 00:29:47.080
the more you feel like you're special.

00:29:48.040 --> 00:29:52.960
Pabongka Rinpoche said, "The whole  All the Dharma you have ever studied in your life, all the things you have memorized,

00:29:52.960 --> 00:29:54.720
all the things you have debated about,

00:29:54.720 --> 00:29:56.800
all the Geshe degrees you have ever been able to obtain

00:29:58.480 --> 00:30:04.160
– you know nothing compared to what remains to be learned.

00:30:04.480 --> 00:30:07.560
You are like a worm at the bottom of the ocean

00:30:08.240 --> 00:30:10.120
that sometimes comes out and looks at the stars.

00:30:13.000 --> 00:30:15.680
Many of these stars are surrounded by planets.

00:30:16.520 --> 00:30:20.440
There are people on these planets.  There are things you need to know about these people.

00:30:21.400 --> 00:30:24.480
There are things that we know,

00:30:24.720 --> 00:30:26.720
that we are so proud to know,

00:30:27.680 --> 00:30:33.880
that are a tiny, very tiny part of what you might know.

00:30:35.160 --> 00:30:37.200
So there is no need to be proud.

00:30:37.200 --> 00:30:39.200
Next.

00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:47.240
One of the main motivations not to break your vows

00:30:47.680 --> 00:30:54.240
or your commitments, your morals, which will stop you from achieving nirvana, which will stop you from achieving the second

00:30:55.080 --> 00:30:57.680
level of lamrim is personal nirvana;

00:30:58.720 --> 00:31:03.000
This is the understanding of emptiness, the study of emptiness.

00:31:04.320 --> 00:31:06.320
If you understand that the bad things

00:31:06.920 --> 00:31:08.920
others do to you

00:31:09.480 --> 00:31:13.240
stem directly from what you did last week,

00:31:13.960 --> 00:31:18.240
then you won't make big mistakes.  The more you can study emptiness,

00:31:19.000 --> 00:31:22.440
the more you can study cause and effect, dependent origination,

00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:25.280
which means this person comes from my seeds,

00:31:26.360 --> 00:31:33.760
the easier it will be to keep your commitments.  The easier it will be.  So study, study, study.

00:31:35.560 --> 00:31:41.320
I had a teacher, an old Mongolian spiritual teacher, very old, sick with tuberculosis, and

00:31:46.800 --> 00:31:48.720
he often said,

00:31:48.720 --> 00:31:56.240
"You are very good. You are so proud, you feel great pride about Princeton and

00:31:57.080 --> 00:31:58.720
then the Geshe degree,

00:31:58.720 --> 00:32:00.800
it is very useful, very useful...

00:32:00.880 --> 00:32:03.960
you will try even harder

00:32:04.440 --> 00:32:06.440
just to look smart.

00:32:06.520 --> 00:32:11.600
That is good, but later try to give it up.

00:32:11.960 --> 00:32:15.080
Just learn to be a good person."  It's very funny

00:32:16.080 --> 00:32:19.000
He gave me Adam's text on his deathbed.

00:32:19.760 --> 00:32:21.760
I remember this.

00:32:24.040 --> 00:32:25.960
Next.  Is

00:32:25.960 --> 00:32:30.320
this technically the fourth reason or not?  No.

00:32:30.440 --> 00:32:35.480
One of the reasons why you break your vows or lose your commitments.

00:32:37.560 --> 00:32:39.680
It is very difficult in today's world to

00:32:40.120 --> 00:32:45.960
remember your vows when you are very busy.  When everything moves very fast.

00:32:46.520 --> 00:32:48.920
There are a thousand things to find on the internet

00:32:49.680 --> 00:32:53.000
and life moves so fast.

00:32:53.440 --> 00:32:58.640
It is difficult to maintain this self-awareness;  Do

00:32:58.640 --> 00:33:03.080
I break my vows, do I do anything to harm others?

00:33:03.840 --> 00:33:08.680
You need to slow down a little, go back to your vows,

00:33:09.080 --> 00:33:14.720
and maintain some conscious sensitivity

00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:19.880
to the fact that you have obligations not to harm other people.

00:33:20.080 --> 00:33:24.160
The more things you have to do, the more attentive you should be.

00:33:25.680 --> 00:33:31.000
It's even easier to get annoyed with your partner when you're very busy.

00:33:31.000 --> 00:33:33.200
They're trying to tell you something and

00:33:33.960 --> 00:33:36.320
you have 10 things to do at work and you're like,

00:33:37.840 --> 00:33:42.120
"I don't have time to listen right now.

00:33:42.800 --> 00:33:45.960
My boss gave me 10 things to do."

00:33:46.440 --> 00:33:48.440
These are the moments when you must slow down

00:33:49.200 --> 00:33:51.200
and return to your vows.

00:33:51.280 --> 00:33:55.000
Don't forget your commitment to be kind to other people, even when you are under

00:33:55.680 --> 00:33:57.680
a lot of stress and are very busy.  It

00:33:59.960 --> 00:34:04.440
is better to break a few business commitments than to be

00:34:05.760 --> 00:34:10.040
nervous and irritable and not be kind to people,

00:34:11.200 --> 00:34:14.040
better to not pay a bill or miss a business meeting or

00:34:15.000 --> 00:34:17.560
not do as good a job as you can

00:34:18.720 --> 00:34:21.960
if it means keeping your mind clear.

00:34:25.080 --> 00:34:27.080
Next picture.

00:34:27.480 --> 00:34:30.840
This is a woman buying a useless thing in a store.

00:34:33.200 --> 00:34:35.200
Try to remember this story.

00:34:36.800 --> 00:34:42.160
She said, "Oh, this box is so beautiful."   She went to the department store.  She bought this.....

00:34:42.600 --> 00:34:44.600
....what is this thing from the home decor store, the

00:34:45.080 --> 00:34:48.480
place where you shop?  Box and Barrel.

00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:54.040
She went to the Crate and Barrel in America.  She said, "Oh, my husband will love this box."

00:34:54.520 --> 00:34:57.480
She has no idea what she'll use it for,

00:34:58.040 --> 00:35:00.040
but she's taking it home.

00:35:04.320 --> 00:35:09.400
Then when she gets home, her husband will say, "You're crazy, that's a useless little box.

00:35:09.400 --> 00:35:15.480
We have enough junk in the house. Take it back. Give me your money back."

00:35:16.920 --> 00:35:20.720
Should she go to the gas station and try to return it?

00:35:24.120 --> 00:35:29.760
No, that's not where she got the box from. This seems obvious, but we have to say it.

00:35:31.480 --> 00:35:33.480
If you buy a stupid box

00:35:34.040 --> 00:35:37.080
because you like it and you think your husband will like it and he doesn't...

00:35:39.000 --> 00:35:41.080
and he talks you into taking the box back.

00:35:42.040 --> 00:35:46.160
Don't take it back to the other place. Take it back to where you bought it.

00:35:46.720 --> 00:35:48.720
What does that mean?

00:35:55.480 --> 00:35:58.080
You guys have to pay me.

00:35:59.680 --> 00:36:01.680
When the time comes to confess

00:36:01.680 --> 00:36:03.480
that you broke the vow,

00:36:03.480 --> 00:36:06.120
try to go back to the person who gave you the vow.

00:36:07.080 --> 00:36:12.120
Try to confess to the person who gave you the vow. Is it okay

00:36:12.200 --> 00:36:15.960
to confess to yourself at home?

00:36:17.680 --> 00:36:21.960
In general, not for vows that you took from other people.

00:36:24.040 --> 00:36:26.040
If you haven't taken the vow

00:36:26.040 --> 00:36:28.600
from someone else, then,  Maybe you can

00:36:29.280 --> 00:36:34.080
confess at home to a Buddha statue or something like that, in extreme cases that's okay.

00:36:34.440 --> 00:36:36.120
But in general,

00:36:36.520 --> 00:36:39.080
if you can go back to the person who gave you the vows

00:36:40.160 --> 00:36:45.200
and confess to them openly, don't be ashamed. We're shameless all day long.

00:36:45.840 --> 00:36:49.080
So be shameless with your vows and say, "What the hell?" -

00:36:49.960 --> 00:36:52.720
go straight to your teacher and tell them you broke this stupid vow.

00:36:53.200 --> 00:36:56.720
And your teacher will say, "Wow, you're really a bad person. You're like that, yeah, yeah."

00:36:57.400 --> 00:37:02.040
Get it over with, and then you'll feel so pure, you'll feel good.

00:37:03.520 --> 00:37:07.320
You can be ashamed of a lot of things in your life, but don't be ashamed of your vows.

00:37:07.320 --> 00:37:11.000
If you break a vow, go and tell somebody,

00:37:11.000 --> 00:37:14.240
and that's how you get rid of it. You get rid of the problem.

00:37:14.520 --> 00:37:20.000
If you hold it in and hide it, and if you do more to hide it than to confess

00:37:20.040 --> 00:37:23.200
or keep it in, then it's just stupid

00:37:23.480 --> 00:37:26.600
and you won't feel good. You don't  you will feel pure.

00:37:27.480 --> 00:37:31.760
Just be open with your teachers. I have this problem. I have this bad habit.

00:37:33.560 --> 00:37:37.720
Karma is destroyed, the seed is destroyed.

00:37:38.320 --> 00:37:44.920
Your teacher will say, "I've heard this before, you told me this before." But be persistent and keep telling them. The

00:37:48.320 --> 00:37:50.320
next picture.

00:37:51.840 --> 00:37:54.320
It's about... wait, do you remember?

00:38:01.160 --> 00:38:04.200
Again, it's about honoring the

00:38:04.800 --> 00:38:07.480
small details of the vows.

00:38:08.400 --> 00:38:13.680
These are actually vows for monks, they had to brush their teeth, with a

00:38:13.680 --> 00:38:16.320
stick called a so shing,

00:38:16.320 --> 00:38:18.440
it was a stick that you had to use to brush your teeth,

00:38:18.600 --> 00:38:21.280
you just cut it from a tree and you use it.

00:38:22.160 --> 00:38:24.160
It's a toothbrush.

00:38:24.320 --> 00:38:29.360
It said that monks had to have their own toothbrushes, and you have to brush your teeth.

00:38:31.840 --> 00:38:34.040
It may seem like a small thing.

00:38:34.920 --> 00:38:38.920
"Wait, I'm trying to keep my tantric vow to go to Amitabha's paradise

00:38:39.560 --> 00:38:43.080
and protect all sentient beings," and the Buddha says, "Yeah, but for now,

00:38:43.080 --> 00:38:46.240
could you just brush your teeth  "Every day?"

00:38:46.240 --> 00:38:49.560
You might think, but it's not such a big vow.

00:38:50.040 --> 00:38:53.800
But it's the little things that make up the Buddha's paradise.

00:38:53.800 --> 00:38:57.680
It's the little things that bodhisattvas do

00:38:58.040 --> 00:39:00.120
that are pleasing to other people.

00:39:01.000 --> 00:39:03.840
Of course, everyone in the world is going to...

00:39:05.080 --> 00:39:09.000
...stop a nuclear war or whatever if they can. I mean, that's obvious.

00:39:10.160 --> 00:39:12.120
But are you a good enough person

00:39:13.200 --> 00:39:15.840
that you don't even want people to smell your breath.

00:39:16.800 --> 00:39:18.360
Maybe it will hurt them?

00:39:18.480 --> 00:39:20.160
If you're very sensitive

00:39:21.080 --> 00:39:23.560
to little things that could hurt other people,

00:39:24.920 --> 00:39:27.200
then we can say that you're keeping your morality.

00:39:28.160 --> 00:39:33.680
And then, it's the little details that put the finishing touches

00:39:34.240 --> 00:39:37.560
on your Buddha's paradise, which you see in the next picture.

00:39:41.480 --> 00:39:46.160
This person is decorating a Christmas tree...

00:39:47.800 --> 00:39:52.240
If you've ever decorated a Christmas tree, but those of us who grew up in the Christian tradition,

00:39:53.000 --> 00:39:55.000
our parents made us decorate Christmas trees.

00:39:55.840 --> 00:39:58.120
There's something cool about

00:39:58.920 --> 00:40:01.800
hanging the last ornament.

00:40:01.800 --> 00:40:06.920
Everyone looks at the tree and says, "Done?"  and then they say, "Yes, it's all ready."

00:40:07.840 --> 00:40:11.480
And he says, "Wait, there's one more ball we have to hang right here."

00:40:12.040 --> 00:40:14.800
That decorating the Christmas tree

00:40:16.040 --> 00:40:22.000
is brushing your teeth. It's the little finishing details

00:40:22.240 --> 00:40:28.720
that you add to your Buddhahood. It's the little things that make Buddhas. It's

00:40:28.720 --> 00:40:32.160
not about the big things. It's not about the big things. It's paying attention

00:40:33.080 --> 00:40:35.000
to the little things

00:40:35.000 --> 00:40:40.120
to make other people happy that makes Buddha.

00:40:41.560 --> 00:40:43.560
Next.

00:40:45.560 --> 00:40:49.040
See if you remember this. I'll give you the key - yamantaka, yamantaka.

00:40:57.000 --> 00:40:59.960
It's a famous lamrim story.

00:41:01.960 --> 00:41:06.040
Monks and nuns are supposed to practice Sojong twice a month and admit

00:41:06.920 --> 00:41:08.920
the mistakes we've made to each other

00:41:09.400 --> 00:41:11.400
and openly.

00:41:13.080 --> 00:41:15.080
The teacher said,

00:41:15.200 --> 00:41:18.320
"...they hit the 'gandhi' stick."  They hit the "gandi".

00:41:19.200 --> 00:41:22.600
It's a special piece of wood, it looks like a 2x4

00:41:23.200 --> 00:41:27.600
and you hit it with another stick and it makes a sharp, dull sound...

00:41:28.160 --> 00:41:33.400
and it's an ancient bell before metal was common.

00:41:33.400 --> 00:41:38.080
They hit the board and when you hear it

00:41:38.240 --> 00:41:41.360
you should go to Sojong.  They still do it.

00:41:41.680 --> 00:41:44.040
I made the "gandhi" stick with my teacher.  He wanted one like this for himself

00:41:45.200 --> 00:41:47.560
and we made it in the right size.

00:41:47.960 --> 00:41:49.600
Here are all these rules.

00:41:49.880 --> 00:41:51.880
When you hear the blow of the gandi stick

00:41:52.240 --> 00:41:54.240
you have to....hold it here..

00:41:54.600 --> 00:41:57.360
You hold the gandi stick here and you hit it like this.

00:41:58.040 --> 00:42:01.200
Then all monks and nuns must come to confession.

00:42:02.120 --> 00:42:05.760
This teacher says, "Hey, they hit Gandhi. Let's go."

00:42:06.520 --> 00:42:09.200
The student replies, "No, I'm not going to confession today."

00:42:10.160 --> 00:42:12.160
The teacher asks: "What?"

00:42:12.440 --> 00:42:17.200
It is one of the main obligations of a monk to practice Sojong.

00:42:17.960 --> 00:42:20.600
The teacher asks: "What are you talking about?"  The student replies: "I don't have to go today."

00:42:21.400 --> 00:42:24.080
The teacher says, "What do you mean you don't have to go today?"

00:42:24.120 --> 00:42:27.920
The student replies: "Have you forgotten that yesterday you gave me the Yamantaka empowerment?

00:42:28.320 --> 00:42:33.080
I am Yamantaka, I am Buddha. I don't need to go to Sojong anymore."

00:42:33.960 --> 00:42:38.160
The teacher grabs him by the ear and says, "What the hell, are you Yamantaka?

00:42:38.280 --> 00:42:43.240
Yamantaka will come with me to Sojong right now."

00:42:44.600 --> 00:42:48.160
This means – don’t tell me that you are a great tantric,

00:42:49.080 --> 00:42:51.640
and you don’t need to observe morality

00:42:51.640 --> 00:42:54.080
and now you have a higher vision –

00:42:54.800 --> 00:42:57.960
this is a completely wrong idea!

00:42:58.920 --> 00:43:02.040
If you have received secret initiation,

00:43:02.600 --> 00:43:05.600
then you must do Sojong or something like that every morning.

00:43:05.840 --> 00:43:08.400
You must practice more than others.

00:43:08.400 --> 00:43:10.760
Because that's what gives you...

00:43:11.000 --> 00:43:14.920
gives power to your tantric practice.  Be kind to other people

00:43:14.920 --> 00:43:16.720
and admit when you make a mistake.

00:43:17.480 --> 00:43:19.480
Next.

00:43:22.520 --> 00:43:29.080
This is a sad picture.  We always think of morality as the basis of

00:43:29.080 --> 00:43:32.120
our practice, the foundation of our practice.

00:43:33.120 --> 00:43:35.960
Pabongka Rinpoche sort of turned this around.

00:43:37.000 --> 00:43:38.800
This is a perfect picture.

00:43:38.800 --> 00:43:42.240
He said, "Imagine an apple tree

00:43:42.440 --> 00:43:46.160
that someone has divided in half. Actually, they used a palm tree.

00:43:47.400 --> 00:43:52.360
Someone divided it, and they cut off the top of the tree.

00:43:52.720 --> 00:43:55.080
So you won't have any leaves, not

00:43:55.360 --> 00:43:58.040
even a single leaf will grow.

00:43:58.320 --> 00:44:00.440
So you won't have any flowers.

00:44:01.480 --> 00:44:05.080
So you won't get the fruits that always come from flowers.

00:44:05.840 --> 00:44:07.880
You won't get anything.

00:44:08.160 --> 00:44:13.560
A person who is not kind to other people, day after day, hour after hour,

00:44:14.800 --> 00:44:18.840
they are depriving themselves of any chance of

00:44:20.160 --> 00:44:23.560
getting these beautiful fruits from the practice.

00:44:23.680 --> 00:44:25.200
Next.

00:44:32.160 --> 00:44:34.920
This was an idea about something my teacher asked me...

00:44:36.800 --> 00:44:42.440
Sorry, I asked my teacher, and I don't know if you remember, but I asked him.

00:44:44.040 --> 00:44:49.200
The first of the five paths, the path of accumulation,

00:44:50.800 --> 00:44:55.440
you attain it when you have personal tragedy,

00:44:55.840 --> 00:44:59.080
but if you are on the bodhisattva path,

00:44:59.400 --> 00:45:01.560
you attain it when you get bodhichitta.

00:45:01.560 --> 00:45:05.680
I asked, "I don't understand, what is tragic about bodhichitta?

00:45:07.000 --> 00:45:09.000
And he said, "No, no, no.

00:45:09.280 --> 00:45:12.440
It's still the theme of tragedy.

00:45:13.000 --> 00:45:19.200
It's just the tragedy of every living being, every being in this entire universe,

00:45:20.120 --> 00:45:22.120
is experiencing the same tragedy."

00:45:23.440 --> 00:45:30.000
This common tragedy is the beginning of the five paths.

00:45:30.160 --> 00:45:32.200
Thinking about this tragedy

00:45:32.520 --> 00:45:35.600
is the beginning of the five paths for the bodhisattva.

00:45:35.600 --> 00:45:37.120
So it's actually the same thing.  The

00:45:37.560 --> 00:45:41.760
puppy is having trouble, but now all the puppies in the basket are having trouble.

00:45:44.040 --> 00:45:46.040
We are all in this together.

00:45:46.040 --> 00:45:48.800
And this is the beginning of bodhicitta.

00:45:50.160 --> 00:45:53.560
Next picture.

00:45:53.560 --> 00:45:58.200
This is a guy shaking hands with someone in his office.

00:45:58.920 --> 00:46:05.200
I suppose the lady is introducing them to each other.  This is Joe, he works in the advertising department,

00:46:05.200 --> 00:46:08.800
and this is Sam, he works in the computer department.

00:46:09.400 --> 00:46:11.400
They shake hands.  Do

00:46:12.040 --> 00:46:14.040
you remember what this is?

00:46:19.000 --> 00:46:24.520
It was a really, really cool exercise where we had to close our eyes

00:46:25.280 --> 00:46:28.160
and think about the person who irritates us the most.

00:46:28.920 --> 00:46:33.120
And see if we can get upset.  The problem with this kind of practice is that

00:46:33.760 --> 00:46:36.240
after about 10 minutes you forget that it is a practice.

00:46:37.080 --> 00:46:39.080
And you really get upset!

00:46:40.160 --> 00:46:42.160
Let's see if I can get upset.

00:46:42.600 --> 00:46:44.160
How are you going to do this?

00:46:44.160 --> 00:46:46.920
I'm going to think about this guy who gave me trouble this week.  "Okay, go ahead."

00:46:48.440 --> 00:46:52.320
Then slowly the man begins to tremble.  You say, "What's going on?"

00:46:52.480 --> 00:46:56.040
"I was upset."  The experiment was a success.

00:46:56.800 --> 00:47:00.400
If this is your lama, they will say,

00:47:01.080 --> 00:47:05.000
"Look how you feel when you first start thinking about this person.

00:47:06.040 --> 00:47:08.600
How do you feel? What's going on in your heart?"  I

00:47:09.480 --> 00:47:13.040
don’t know about you, but I have a little lump in my heart.

00:47:13.080 --> 00:47:17.960
I'm starting to feel some discomfort here or there.

00:47:18.600 --> 00:47:23.080
When I think about a person who is bothering me or about a problem that is bothering me,

00:47:23.680 --> 00:47:27.480
I can deliberately build up tension

00:47:27.760 --> 00:47:29.760
within myself.

00:47:30.120 --> 00:47:36.920
He says, "Let's do an exercise - let's try to create some tension in your heart,

00:47:37.280 --> 00:47:42.040
then look at that tension and recognize it, as if you were shaking someone's hand.

00:47:43.000 --> 00:47:46.600
Find out what it feels like

00:47:47.000 --> 00:47:50.040
when a mental cloud, a negative emotion,

00:47:51.000 --> 00:47:54.240
appears in your heart, and keep practicing this.

00:47:55.200 --> 00:47:58.040
Once you feel better and you've forgotten about that person,

00:47:58.040 --> 00:47:59.200
then think of them again.

00:48:00.200 --> 00:48:01.520
See if you can get upset again.

00:48:01.520 --> 00:48:03.360
See if you start getting upset again.

00:48:04.040 --> 00:48:08.840
Try to get familiar with what it feels like; shake hands: 'Hello.'  This is Geshe Michael."

00:48:08.840 --> 00:48:10.320
"Hello.  "What, what's your name?"

00:48:11.080 --> 00:48:14.080
"I'm starting to get upset with this man."

00:48:14.080 --> 00:48:17.000
"Nice to meet you.  Now I know what you look like.

00:48:17.680 --> 00:48:21.200
Now I can look after you.  I can avoid you in the future."

00:48:21.840 --> 00:48:23.840
Next.

00:48:28.240 --> 00:48:30.920
It's called "journey to the center of the sun."

00:48:33.000 --> 00:48:37.960
The theme of this lamrim was - Love in the Time of a Virus. A

00:48:41.080 --> 00:48:44.320
virus is a big thing, it's spread all over the world.

00:48:45.000 --> 00:48:48.320
I've lived a long life and I thought I've seen it all.

00:48:49.080 --> 00:48:54.960
I turned 60 and I thought nothing new would happen now.

00:48:55.120 --> 00:48:57.400
I'm quite prepared for anything that can happen.

00:48:58.320 --> 00:49:06.040
I've seen everything, and nothing can upset me too much. Then this virus comes along and threatens everyone in the world.

00:49:06.600 --> 00:49:11.080
It's a big thing that covers the whole planet.

00:49:13.560 --> 00:49:17.000
I don't know if this has happened to you, but it has happened to me.

00:49:17.280 --> 00:49:22.480
This is probably bad deed number nine, which is ill will;

00:49:23.480 --> 00:49:25.680
being happy when someone has problems.

00:49:25.680 --> 00:49:31.160
When I heard about famous, annoying people getting sick.

00:49:32.120 --> 00:49:37.080
I didn't want them to die or anything, but...

00:49:37.960 --> 00:49:42.280
...I said it's bad to be bad.

00:49:43.000 --> 00:49:46.040
And then I caught myself thinking about it. It

00:49:47.080 --> 00:49:49.120
feels like a big thing. It

00:49:49.480 --> 00:49:56.120
feels like,  that this problem has spread all over the planet.

00:49:57.080 --> 00:50:02.040
It feels like I'm having a hard time dealing with it.

00:50:02.520 --> 00:50:04.520
We've just started,

00:50:04.600 --> 00:50:06.800
after 10 years of studying in lam-rim,

00:50:08.040 --> 00:50:12.840
we've just entered the path of people with great abilities.

00:50:13.840 --> 00:50:16.800
We're going to open this teaching

00:50:18.160 --> 00:50:21.200
with the idea of ​​bodhichitta. What is bodhichitta?

00:50:21.280 --> 00:50:27.000
It's not the enlightened mind. Forget this lousy translation, incredibly bad translation.

00:50:27.960 --> 00:50:34.520
It's the wish that I could become a Buddha to help countless sentient beings.

00:50:35.760 --> 00:50:37.960
There is a direct experience of this,

00:50:38.520 --> 00:50:41.600
just as there is a direct perception of emptiness.

00:50:41.600 --> 00:50:46.920
There are parallel experiences that

00:50:47.000 --> 00:50:53.080
we have to have in this life, and again, you have to be in meditation.

00:50:54.040 --> 00:51:00.960
We're describing an extraordinary... what do you call it?... breakthrough.

00:51:02.400 --> 00:51:06.040
The experience of the threshold of entry,

00:51:07.080 --> 00:51:11.720
when you enter a deep state of meditation.

00:51:11.960 --> 00:51:15.480
Because time and space come from seeds,

00:51:15.760 --> 00:51:17.760
if you can deal with these seeds,

00:51:18.040 --> 00:51:20.720
then you can compress time and space.

00:51:21.480 --> 00:51:25.080
In a meditation that lasts no more than half an hour.

00:51:26.520 --> 00:51:28.520
You can actually meet

00:51:28.720 --> 00:51:30.800
every person in the universe,

00:51:31.720 --> 00:51:34.440
including  animals and insects, birds and fish.

00:51:35.080 --> 00:51:39.400
You can talk to each of them individually,

00:51:40.040 --> 00:51:42.040
for half an hour.

00:51:42.120 --> 00:51:44.920
You can make a commitment to each of them.

00:51:45.560 --> 00:51:50.160
You meet with them, you see that each of them is suffering,

00:51:50.400 --> 00:51:55.840
each of them is going through a difficult life and is worried about the future.

00:51:56.400 --> 00:51:58.320
You can go to each one individually and say,

00:51:59.080 --> 00:52:01.880
"I'll take care of everything, calm down."

00:52:02.160 --> 00:52:04.560
I worked when I was at university.

00:52:05.280 --> 00:52:08.440
I got a scholarship, but they told me I had to work a few hours a week. It

00:52:09.000 --> 00:52:11.000
turned out to be 30 hours a week.

00:52:12.160 --> 00:52:15.200
I had to drive a truck.

00:52:16.320 --> 00:52:21.200
Actually, at first they put me in the cafeteria and said you will be mopping the floor in the cafeteria.

00:52:21.280 --> 00:52:24.920
I quit within 10 hours. I quit on the first day.

00:52:25.960 --> 00:52:29.760
Then they said you can drive a truck. I said, this is fun. I will drive a truck.

00:52:30.800 --> 00:52:33.520
I drove a truck for five years.

00:52:35.200 --> 00:52:37.560
We had a guy, a

00:52:37.960 --> 00:52:42.960
regular at the university, named Big John.

00:52:43.320 --> 00:52:49.240
His name was Big John. He's Polish, seven feet tall, a huge guy.

00:52:50.800 --> 00:52:52.400
All  They were afraid when they saw him.

00:52:52.400 --> 00:52:56.120
They were afraid of him, but he was a very kind person.

00:52:57.000 --> 00:53:02.840
He brought donuts to work and was from Trenton, New Jersey.

00:53:04.920 --> 00:53:10.320
He did the nicest things for us and covered for us. One time we wrecked the truck.

00:53:11.000 --> 00:53:13.840
We crashed the truck into a tree and broke it in half.

00:53:14.440 --> 00:53:19.560
He covered for us: "Oh, those bolts weren't tight enough.

00:53:19.560 --> 00:53:23.400
I don't know what happened.  The truck fell apart.  Don't blame these guys.

00:53:24.160 --> 00:53:26.160
Don't blame these young guys.

00:53:26.440 --> 00:53:28.440
They're just drivers."

00:53:28.920 --> 00:53:33.080
Then he winked at us and said, "I've got your back.  I've got your back, guys."

00:53:33.680 --> 00:53:37.040
I always think of him when I think about bodhichitta.

00:53:37.680 --> 00:53:42.000
You'll meet every living being in the universe face to face.

00:53:42.600 --> 00:53:46.600
And you'll say, "Big John's got your back.  I've got your back.  Don't worry."

00:53:47.200 --> 00:53:49.280
Don't worry about it. I've got your back.

00:53:50.320 --> 00:53:52.880
That's bodhichitta. You have to have that experience.

00:53:52.880 --> 00:53:55.680
You have to work for that experience. You have to meditate.

00:53:56.240 --> 00:53:58.080
You have to study bodhichitta. You have to

00:53:58.080 --> 00:54:00.320
study the lam-rim about bodhichitta.

00:54:01.360 --> 00:54:03.400
You have to do all these steps;

00:54:04.480 --> 00:54:06.480
exchanging yourself for others...

00:54:07.000 --> 00:54:11.120
One day you'll have that experience and meet every living being.

00:54:11.840 --> 00:54:15.280
You'll tell them, "I've got your back." Don't worry. I've got your back."

00:54:15.400 --> 00:54:20.040
Big Mike will take care of you, or Big Tim, or Big Saiji.  Do

00:54:20.600 --> 00:54:22.600
n't worry.  Do

00:54:23.080 --> 00:54:25.480
n't worry.  I'll take care of it!

00:54:26.440 --> 00:54:30.040
It's exactly what it sounds like.  This is a personal commitment.

00:54:31.280 --> 00:54:33.280
Why are we talking about this?

00:54:33.840 --> 00:54:37.560
You will do this for countless worlds.  When you do this, the day you do this,

00:54:38.040 --> 00:54:40.520
you will be doing this for countless worlds.

00:54:42.160 --> 00:54:48.320
An action that is performed directly on every living being in countless worlds will have

00:54:49.400 --> 00:54:54.160
no problem taking care of one virus in one world.

00:54:54.320 --> 00:54:55.440
It's nothing.  A

00:54:55.760 --> 00:54:57.760
virus that puts

00:54:58.600 --> 00:55:03.680
7 or 8 billion people at risk is nothing compared to bodhichitta.

00:55:04.960 --> 00:55:08.600
We said, if you spill ketchup on your shirt

00:55:08.600 --> 00:55:15.280
and you take that shirt into the middle of the sun where it's 25 million degrees Fahrenheit, the

00:55:15.760 --> 00:55:18.720
ketchup stain will probably come out.

00:55:19.400 --> 00:55:24.240
You probably don't need to worry about the ketchup stain.  Work on your bodhichitta.

00:55:25.400 --> 00:55:29.000
You will destroy the virus, inadvertently, by accident.

00:55:29.760 --> 00:55:31.760
Nothing special.

00:55:32.120 --> 00:55:34.120
Next picture.

00:55:35.560 --> 00:55:38.120
Don't get involved with other paths.

00:55:38.920 --> 00:55:41.480
Learn bodhicitta.  Learn to gain this experience.

00:55:42.240 --> 00:55:44.240
Don't waste your time.

00:55:45.000 --> 00:55:47.680
Don't focus on other things.  Focus on bodhichitta.

00:55:48.800 --> 00:55:51.200
Then you won't have to do things twice.

00:55:51.560 --> 00:55:55.200
We were talking about when things are done twice.  This lady is in a great hurry.

00:55:55.680 --> 00:55:58.440
She says, "I don't have time for this bodhicitta.

00:55:59.000 --> 00:56:01.840
I'll go straight to tantra."

00:56:02.600 --> 00:56:06.120
You will still have to go back and pick up the thing you forgot,

00:56:06.120 --> 00:56:07.080
namely, bodhicitta.

00:56:07.080 --> 00:56:09.360
First, work on your bodhichitta.

00:56:10.440 --> 00:56:16.160
You don't have to go home, pick up bodhichitta and come back.

00:56:20.320 --> 00:56:23.760
Next we had a radical example in the next idiom.

00:56:29.000 --> 00:56:33.080
She is difficult to remember.  I'll give you a second to think about it.  I

00:56:43.840 --> 00:56:45.840
don't know if you remember this.

00:56:48.040 --> 00:56:49.720
It's quite complicated.

00:56:49.720 --> 00:56:59.160
A group of 60 boys and girls were going to achieve nirvana by simply seeing emptiness directly,

00:56:59.320 --> 00:57:02.040
without bodhichitta, this is the lower nirvana.

00:57:03.680 --> 00:57:09.400
Manjushri appears and teaches them bodhicitta.

00:57:09.520 --> 00:57:12.360
Maybe he talked about this experience we just talked about.

00:57:14.720 --> 00:57:18.920
They were all irritated with Manjushri.  They're like, "Don't waste our time.

00:57:18.920 --> 00:57:22.160
We're close to nirvana. We can feel it. We can taste it.

00:57:22.920 --> 00:57:25.680
We've all seen emptiness before, don't waste our time.

00:57:27.080 --> 00:57:31.160
Don't talk to us about it."

00:57:32.920 --> 00:57:37.520
Because they did not respect the teaching of bodhichitta,

00:57:37.760 --> 00:57:42.160
they went to hell.

00:57:43.080 --> 00:57:46.040
They did not reach nirvana.  They fell into the realms of hell.

00:57:47.080 --> 00:57:49.080
But they burned everything

00:57:50.040 --> 00:57:55.560
and they became people again after many millions of years.

00:57:57.840 --> 00:58:03.560
Deep within them was this teaching that Manjushri had given them about bodhichitta, and they remembered it.

00:58:04.240 --> 00:58:07.680
They became bodhisattvas and became Buddhas.

00:58:08.600 --> 00:58:10.600
It will take less time than

00:58:12.320 --> 00:58:16.320
achieving lower nirvana without studying bodhichitta.  It would be

00:58:16.800 --> 00:58:20.800
faster to go to hell

00:58:20.800 --> 00:58:22.440
and come back

00:58:22.440 --> 00:58:25.080
and start all over again with bodhichitta

00:58:25.960 --> 00:58:27.880
if you didn't use bodhichitta

00:58:27.880 --> 00:58:29.960
and ended up in lower nirvana.

00:58:32.520 --> 00:58:37.120
This is an image of someone deliberately sending someone else the wrong way.

00:58:38.720 --> 00:58:41.000
This lady asks,

00:58:41.000 --> 00:58:44.240
"Where is the super highway that leads to the store I want to visit?"

00:58:45.000 --> 00:58:48.480
The guy knows the highway is closed.

00:58:48.720 --> 00:58:52.240
He tells her: "Don't turn there, the highway is closed. You need to go the other way."

00:58:53.000 --> 00:58:55.000
And she insists: “No,

00:58:55.400 --> 00:58:57.400
tell me where the highway I need is.”

00:58:58.040 --> 00:58:59.840
Then he deceives her

00:58:59.840 --> 00:59:06.120
and says: "Take this path."  This is actually a long way that he proposed one way or another.

00:59:07.560 --> 00:59:10.600
This is a story about clever means.

00:59:10.600 --> 00:59:12.160
Next picture.

00:59:17.280 --> 00:59:21.400
This is a warm-up before the race.

00:59:23.560 --> 00:59:27.560
What do we usually use this image for?  Do you remember, guys?

00:59:29.000 --> 00:59:31.040
This is a breathing meditation.

00:59:31.400 --> 00:59:36.800
We usually say that breathing meditation is just a warm-up.  Don't think it's a race.  There is

00:59:37.960 --> 00:59:44.160
no pre-race stretching competition at the Olympics.

00:59:44.160 --> 00:59:48.440
This doesn't happen; they don't give a gold medal for stretching.

00:59:49.400 --> 00:59:54.480
In this case, we are not talking about breathing meditation.  We are talking about the fact that

00:59:54.640 --> 00:59:59.840
it is good to do the three main paths in order.

01:00:01.080 --> 01:00:03.080
To grieve for this world.

01:00:05.960 --> 01:00:09.120
Strive to directly gain this experience of bodhichitta.

01:00:09.800 --> 01:00:12.680
See the void so you can help everyone.

01:00:13.160 --> 01:00:18.880
Do a warm-up with the first feelings of sadness about this life.

01:00:19.000 --> 01:00:21.440
Next picture.

01:00:24.040 --> 01:00:29.960
We're almost done.  I think we are very close.  Are we close yet?  Not that close.  Okay,

01:00:32.040 --> 01:00:35.760
you remember who these guys are, they are a very disgusting company.

01:00:36.520 --> 01:00:41.200
I guess you see them in shopping malls or somewhere else singing bad songs.

01:00:45.080 --> 01:00:47.000
They are called "prelude".

01:00:47.760 --> 01:00:49.760
Steps on the path for practitioners of lesser ability;

01:00:51.200 --> 01:00:53.120
who are trying to achieve a higher rebirth.

01:00:53.120 --> 01:00:55.560
Steps on the path for practitioners of average ability

01:00:56.160 --> 01:00:58.160
who try not to return to this world at all.

01:00:59.080 --> 01:01:02.120
Steps on the Path for Practitioners of Great Ability.

01:01:02.120 --> 01:01:03.080
These two levels are just a prelude.  The

01:01:03.840 --> 01:01:10.440
most important thing is to achieve bodhicitta.  What is higher than bodhicitta?

01:01:13.280 --> 01:01:16.720
There are six perfections.  Check again:

01:01:19.000 --> 01:01:21.000
steps on the path to avoid falling into the

01:01:21.200 --> 01:01:25.800
lower hell realms, steps on the path to attain nirvana,

01:01:26.920 --> 01:01:29.080
and then we get bodhicitta.

01:01:29.240 --> 01:01:30.320
This experience of meeting every living being

01:01:30.320 --> 01:01:35.400
and making a commitment that I will take care of you.  There are

01:01:36.120 --> 01:01:38.120
six up here.

01:01:38.120 --> 01:01:41.080
This is six in Chinese.

01:01:42.160 --> 01:01:45.400
Here are six perfections.

01:01:46.240 --> 01:01:47.400
So what is the most important thing from this?

01:01:47.400 --> 01:01:52.240
Which one is a real group?  What prelude?

01:01:54.920 --> 01:01:56.920
These guys, obviously, lower nirvana is not that important.

01:01:57.680 --> 01:01:59.680
Interestingly, Pabongka Rinpoche says

01:02:00.680 --> 01:02:03.480
that this experience

01:02:04.120 --> 01:02:06.120
with every living being is the

01:02:06.240 --> 01:02:07.400
main action.

01:02:07.400 --> 01:02:09.120
This is what I want you to focus on.

01:02:09.120 --> 01:02:11.200
I want you to try to get this experience.

01:02:12.160 --> 01:02:16.040
If you have this experience, we can talk about the six perfections,

01:02:16.040 --> 01:02:19.960
including number six - the vision of emptiness.

01:02:20.600 --> 01:02:22.600
Let's talk about this later.

01:02:23.080 --> 01:02:26.040
Come on, I want you guys to focus on this experience.

01:02:27.000 --> 01:02:33.080
By the way, a good way to get this experience is to imagine the experience and try to listen to its description.

01:02:34.040 --> 01:02:36.920
Pretend you can do it and keep pretending.

01:02:37.680 --> 01:02:39.200
Keep doing this.

01:02:39.200 --> 01:02:44.160
It looks like a slot machine.

01:02:44.440 --> 01:02:46.560
I like to compare it to a slot machine.

01:02:47.640 --> 01:02:49.560
When you click on a slot machine,

01:02:50.040 --> 01:02:52.040
pictures, cherries and other things start popping up

01:02:52.720 --> 01:02:54.280
.

01:02:54.280 --> 01:02:58.800
Not that I've ever played a slot machine... Well, once, with my dad.

01:02:59.840 --> 01:03:02.840
You press the lever and then these dials start popping out.

01:03:02.840 --> 01:03:04.800
Just imagine

01:03:04.920 --> 01:03:06.920
your mother's face appearing.

01:03:07.760 --> 01:03:12.520
You say, "Mom, you look worried."  She's like, "Yeah, I'm worried about life."

01:03:12.520 --> 01:03:16.480
You say, "Don't worry, Big John's got your back.

01:03:16.840 --> 01:03:19.200
Just calm down. I get it. I'll take care of you."

01:03:20.040 --> 01:03:22.040
Then your father's face appears.

01:03:23.000 --> 01:03:27.360
Not just a picture, but a person appears.

01:03:27.760 --> 01:03:31.360
It's like meditation.  Try to imagine this.  Try practicing this.

01:03:31.560 --> 01:03:33.560
This will trigger something very important.

01:03:34.320 --> 01:03:37.280
This will trigger something very important.  Introduce people one by one.

01:03:38.040 --> 01:03:40.040
See how they feel.

01:03:40.040 --> 01:03:43.160
Make a commitment.  Don't worry.  I've got your back.  I will take care of you.

01:03:43.160 --> 01:03:45.200
Then they leave.  Imagine another person.

01:03:46.240 --> 01:03:49.480
Practice this way.  You can do five or six people.

01:03:50.520 --> 01:03:54.080
It will happen faster because time will change.

01:03:54.600 --> 01:04:00.040
Pabongka Rinpoche says this is the main show.

01:04:01.000 --> 01:04:02.800
This is the Rolling Stones.

01:04:03.080 --> 01:04:09.240
The rest are just new bands that aren't very good.

01:04:10.520 --> 01:04:13.960
Who's at the end?  Do they have a final act?  Usually not.

01:04:14.800 --> 01:04:18.920
Anyway, the rest of them just leave the stadium or something.  Do not worry about it.

01:04:20.600 --> 01:04:22.600
Now we move on to

01:04:23.200 --> 01:04:26.480
10 cool things that will happen to you if you have bodhichitta.

01:04:26.640 --> 01:04:30.040
We will only have time to do the first one in this lamrim.

01:04:30.440 --> 01:04:33.280
The first cool thing about having bodhichitta is...

01:04:34.040 --> 01:04:36.320
if you were a nerdy kid

01:04:37.280 --> 01:04:39.280
who played tennis in school.

01:04:39.960 --> 01:04:42.840
Your dream would be to be on the team.

01:04:43.120 --> 01:04:44.440
Next picture.

01:04:47.640 --> 01:04:50.000
Yes, Geshe Michael is standing in the center.

01:04:50.000 --> 01:04:52.880
Above, not down there.

01:04:54.320 --> 01:05:00.800
You can be on the team.  It's great to be on a team of bodhisattvas.

01:05:02.600 --> 01:05:04.600
Work in this team.

01:05:04.720 --> 01:05:09.000
It's so cool to be on this team

01:05:09.400 --> 01:05:11.840
because this team spans the entire universe.

01:05:12.440 --> 01:05:16.960
These are all the cool people in the entire universe.  It's nice to be part of this team.

01:05:17.080 --> 01:05:18.760
This is very nice.

01:05:19.560 --> 01:05:24.120
This was the first benefit of bodhicitta.

01:05:24.680 --> 01:05:25.920
Next picture.

01:05:28.160 --> 01:05:30.320
This is a guy visiting an art museum.

01:05:32.920 --> 01:05:38.640
He spoke of two levels of tantra;  The first level is meeting with angels, the

01:05:39.960 --> 01:05:43.320
second level is learning from them how to be an angel and how to become an angel.

01:05:43.320 --> 01:05:44.800
On the first level,

01:05:45.680 --> 01:05:47.680
we must actually meet

01:05:48.120 --> 01:05:50.120
real angels in person.

01:05:50.720 --> 01:05:58.720
It's not like standing in an art museum and looking at a statue or thangka of a person.

01:05:59.040 --> 01:06:05.720
This is a meeting with a person directly and this is a completely different matter.

01:06:07.280 --> 01:06:09.720
If you try to practice tantra

01:06:10.080 --> 01:06:15.480
without this experience of bodhichitta, it will be like looking at images of Buddhas

01:06:15.480 --> 01:06:17.400
instead of meeting Buddhas.

01:06:17.720 --> 01:06:22.960
They don't like to talk to people who don't have bodhichitta.

01:06:22.960 --> 01:06:24.320
They feel more comfortable

01:06:24.520 --> 01:06:28.040
around people who have had this experience.  Try to get this experience.

01:06:28.600 --> 01:06:30.280
Then tantra will work for you.

01:06:30.280 --> 01:06:32.160
If you don't have this experience,

01:06:32.200 --> 01:06:34.360
tantra will be difficult.

01:06:34.360 --> 01:06:39.200
It will be like looking at pictures of Buddhas instead of hanging out with Buddhas.

01:06:40.040 --> 01:06:42.040
Next.

01:06:45.280 --> 01:06:51.120
If you try to practice tantra without bodhichitta, you may get bad results.

01:06:51.320 --> 01:06:54.200
We talked about the first nuclear test

01:06:54.440 --> 01:06:56.480
in our time.

01:06:59.080 --> 01:07:04.800
Scientists have acknowledged that this explosion

01:07:04.920 --> 01:07:07.480
could have burned down the entire world.

01:07:07.480 --> 01:07:09.840
They were just trying to do something cool.

01:07:10.920 --> 01:07:13.600
But they risked a huge disaster.

01:07:14.240 --> 01:07:17.680
This is tantra without bodhichitta.

01:07:18.040 --> 01:07:23.720
It would be like accidentally setting the entire sky on fire.  You'll ruin everything.

01:07:23.960 --> 01:07:25.680
Next.

01:07:28.120 --> 01:07:32.880
Even a small amount of neutral karma

01:07:33.040 --> 01:07:36.960
will become powerful for a person with bodhichitta.

01:07:37.080 --> 01:07:39.080
A person with bodhichitta can feed a bird,

01:07:39.400 --> 01:07:41.440
pray about it,

01:07:41.600 --> 01:07:46.840
and it touches millions of people.  They have this power.

01:07:46.840 --> 01:07:48.600
Next picture.

01:07:51.680 --> 01:07:59.120
Even small bad actions, such as stealing French fries to give to a bird, can become positive if performed by a bodhisattva.

01:08:00.600 --> 01:08:08.040
But this is a dangerous practice.  We are not at that level.  We are not at that level.  We are not at that level. Did

01:08:08.720 --> 01:08:10.720
you hear that?  No?

01:08:10.800 --> 01:08:12.800
We had a photo of a

01:08:13.400 --> 01:08:15.400
puffer fish.

01:08:16.040 --> 01:08:21.200
People in Japan, such as macho men, eat this fish.

01:08:22.040 --> 01:08:28.040
It has very, very poisonous parts that can kill you instantly.  In Japan, 50 people die every year.

01:08:29.080 --> 01:08:34.080
But people still go to the restaurant.  To serve this fish in a restaurant,

01:08:34.720 --> 01:08:38.240
you need three years of special training, otherwise you'll kill someone.

01:08:39.080 --> 01:08:42.120
It's like stealing French fries to give to a bird

01:08:43.400 --> 01:08:45.200
because you want to help the bird.

01:08:45.200 --> 01:08:51.240
We are not at that level.  Do not attempt to eat pufferfish unless you are trained.

01:08:52.440 --> 01:08:54.440
Then we had a nice photo of Nick and Erin

01:08:54.920 --> 01:08:58.120
with their big boss,

01:08:59.080 --> 01:09:01.360
Amelie.

01:09:02.120 --> 01:09:04.320
Amelie represents Buddha,

01:09:05.480 --> 01:09:06.800
Nick

01:09:06.800 --> 01:09:08.800
represents the father

01:09:09.400 --> 01:09:14.240
which is bodhichitta, and Erin represents wisdom

01:09:14.440 --> 01:09:16.920
which is the direct perception of emptiness.

01:09:16.920 --> 01:09:18.920
In a certain sense,

01:09:20.800 --> 01:09:25.800
for some reason I don't know what kind of belief it is in Asia, but in a certain sense the father is irreplaceable.  There is something

01:09:28.040 --> 01:09:30.040
special about this father.

01:09:33.400 --> 01:09:35.400
I don't know what this is.  But still...

01:09:36.960 --> 01:09:39.840
Emptiness can be seen on different levels,

01:09:40.600 --> 01:09:42.800
on all three tracks.

01:09:43.480 --> 01:09:46.240
But bodhicitta, you have to be a special person.

01:09:47.080 --> 01:09:49.080
You can only see it on the highest track.

01:09:49.760 --> 01:09:51.680
This defines you

01:09:51.680 --> 01:09:53.680
as a person on the top track.

01:09:54.120 --> 01:09:57.600
You need both to have a child who is a Buddha.

01:09:59.080 --> 01:10:01.080
Next picture.

01:10:04.440 --> 01:10:10.040
We said @

01:10:10.600 --> 01:10:13.680
Which Tim identified correctly today.

01:10:14.720 --> 01:10:21.600
What is your main practice?   What is most important in your life right now?

01:10:21.600 --> 01:10:27.360
Until the next lamrim, the Medicine Buddha lamrim...

01:10:28.040 --> 01:10:31.600
....I want you guys to consider this as your main practice.

01:10:31.600 --> 01:10:34.320
Try to have this experience of meeting countless beings.

01:10:34.320 --> 01:10:36.800
Try to get this experience.

01:10:36.800 --> 01:10:40.040
I don't care if you sit for hour after hour and nothing happens,

01:10:40.920 --> 01:10:42.920
just try, just pretend.

01:10:43.080 --> 01:10:47.080
Scroll this through your mind until the next lamrim.

01:10:47.080 --> 01:10:51.200
Let's make a deal like this.  Make this your main practice.

01:10:52.120 --> 01:10:54.120
Next picture.

01:10:56.240 --> 01:11:02.600
If this practice were not so important, then one of the greatest Buddhists of all time, Lord Atisha, would not have sailed to India for

01:11:02.800 --> 01:11:06.240
13 months, risking his life, to receive the teachings on

01:11:06.880 --> 01:11:08.880
bodhichitta that you just received

01:11:09.080 --> 01:11:12.920
in this video.  And you didn't have to go anywhere.

01:11:13.840 --> 01:11:18.920
If Atisha thought it was worth risking his life for 13 months

01:11:19.840 --> 01:11:21.680
on a tiny ship,

01:11:21.680 --> 01:11:25.760
in the Pacific and the Indian Ocean, then maybe

01:11:26.440 --> 01:11:30.040
it matters, maybe it's worth it.

01:11:30.040 --> 01:11:31.560
Next picture.

01:11:34.800 --> 01:11:40.240
I think the stupidest thing you can do in your life is to go to Paris and not buy a croissant.

01:11:41.680 --> 01:11:46.440
Fine.  I'm just saying that there are probably other stupid things you can do in your life.

01:11:46.760 --> 01:11:48.920
But for me it would be absolute stupidity to

01:11:48.920 --> 01:11:52.800
go to Paris and not stop by a bakery.  At least

01:11:54.040 --> 01:11:55.840
buy a pancake

01:11:55.840 --> 01:11:57.840
on the street

01:11:57.960 --> 01:12:00.200
with... what is this chocolate thing?

01:12:02.800 --> 01:12:04.320
Nutella, yes.

01:12:04.320 --> 01:12:06.320
Not trying a pancake with Nutella.

01:12:07.000 --> 01:12:12.760
Going to Paris and not trying a Nutella crepe is proof you're crazy.

01:12:15.040 --> 01:12:17.200
If you study lamrim,

01:12:17.400 --> 01:12:21.960
if you have advanced this far in lamrim, and Geshela has been teaching it for 10 years,

01:12:22.800 --> 01:12:25.400
you have finally reached the croissant,

01:12:26.040 --> 01:12:28.040
which is the bodhisattva experience.

01:12:28.720 --> 01:12:35.960
Don't go crazy and leave Paris without eating it.  Do not leave lamrim without having this experience.

01:12:36.160 --> 01:12:38.040
You will be a complete idiot.

01:12:41.680 --> 01:12:46.080
We're done with the croissant.  I think you want to give a presentation?

01:12:48.320 --> 01:12:52.040
No, I assumed there might be a croissant in this bag?

01:12:54.320 --> 01:12:56.320
Tim Lowenhaupt

01:12:57.080 --> 01:12:59.560
is going to do the official presentation

01:13:00.800 --> 01:13:02.720
for Heschel, at my expense,

01:13:03.840 --> 01:13:07.400
Oh, is that kraussan?  What do you call it?

01:13:10.520 --> 01:13:12.520
What is it called?

01:13:14.320 --> 01:13:18.560
Kraussan with chocolate!  (Pain au chocolat) You have to cut it into three pieces.

01:13:20.120 --> 01:13:22.320
And give me all three, that is, no, just one.

01:13:23.760 --> 01:13:26.080
I got a chocolate croissant.

01:13:27.000 --> 01:13:30.240
This is what you give to your teacher when he teaches you bodhicitta.

01:13:31.080 --> 01:13:33.200
Let's make a deal.

01:13:34.160 --> 01:13:36.040


01:13:37.000 --> 01:13:41.760
Work on this experience for the next couple of months.  Do the dedication chapter in your Shantideva meditation.

01:13:43.680 --> 01:13:48.600
Try to work on getting this experience.  The worst that can happen is that at least

01:13:49.400 --> 01:13:52.440
you will have planted the seeds in your mind to have that experience.

01:13:53.280 --> 01:13:55.080
Just pretend.

01:13:55.080 --> 01:13:59.680
Just sit and fantasize about it.  Fantasy is a good meditation.

01:14:00.880 --> 01:14:03.000
Imagine that you had this experience of meeting,

01:14:03.840 --> 01:14:05.080
one after another,

01:14:05.080 --> 01:14:06.640
every living being.

01:14:06.640 --> 01:14:10.160
You make a personal commitment with each of them

01:14:10.800 --> 01:14:13.400
to take care of them fully,

01:14:14.160 --> 01:14:18.080
Excellent.  See you in the next Medicine Buddha lamrim.  Hooray!

